    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7147" root="حجب" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْجُوبٌ</span></b>  [pass. part. n. of 1]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلِكٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْجُوبٌ</span> (A) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحَجَّبٌ</span></b>  (S) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْتَجبٌ</span></b> 
(A) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحُوْجَبٌ</span></b>  (TA) [<i>A king secluded,</i> or
<i>concealed,</i> from the people]. And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِمْرَأَةٌ مَحْجُوبَةٌ</span>
<i>A woman veiled,</i> or <i>concealed by a curtain</i> or <i>the
like.</i> (TA.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ مَحْجُوبٌ عِنِ الخَيْرِ</span> [<i>He is
debarred from good.</i>] (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  (assumed tropical:)  <i>Blind;</i> (S,
K;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحَوْجَبٌ</span></b> . (TA.)

